;; ============================================================
;; HOWL test harness
;;
;; What is testable today is the VERDICT DISCIPLINE (§6.2) and the
;; structural invariants — the reasoning pipeline is still M0/M1.
;;
;; These are not placeholder tests. §10 item 4 calls the verdict rule a
;; SAFETY property and says to test it by trying to break it, in all
;; three rows, because the failure modes are opposite: folding
;; `inconclusive` into `coherent` gives CI a false pass, and folding it
;; into `incoherent` makes every ontology with an unsupported construct
;; look broken and trains users to ignore the gate.
;;
;; The sharpest row is #2 below — a finding under PARTIAL coverage is
;; still definitive, because inference is monotone. An earlier draft of
;; the spec got exactly that row wrong, sending every out-of-profile run
;; to inconclusive and thereby discarding a sound result.
;; ============================================================

(module test
  (@doc "Verdict-discipline and structural-invariant tests")

